\title{What drain costs in each L1D state}
\taxon{Card}
\tag{card}
\meta{anki}{1786316439363}

\prompt{At drain, what does the head [[UNB6]] entry do for each L1D [[30XT]] state — M/E, S, or miss?}{
  \ul{
    \li{\strong{M or E} — write directly; no fabric transaction at all, since E#{\to}M is a silent upgrade.}
    \li{\strong{S} — issue the Upgrade/GetM now if the speculative one didn't land, and stall until permission arrives.}
    \li{\strong{Miss} — issue GetM to fetch the data and invalidate sharers, allocate an [[89LS]], stall.}
  }

  Drain is decoupled from commit and, under [[VH8Y]], in order — so a stalled head blocks younger senior stores even when their lines are already in M.
}
